# EASM core rules

Durable facts and commands live in `AGENTS.md`. Shipping detail is `docs/shipping.md`. Workflows are the skills under `.cursor/skills/`. Do not repeat those here.

## Before any work

- Run the live preview gate with the `local-setup` skill, and again after every branch switch. Do not edit, install or commit until both sites have loaded in Cursor's browser and you have said "Preview ready, starting work".
- Laravel Herd on Windows is the only local set-up (`https://easm.test`, PHP 8.3 through FastCGI, MySQL 8.4). Never suggest containers, virtual machines, `php artisan serve`, Laragon or any other local stack.
- Ask before running migrations or changing Herd's sites, services or `.env`.

## Ship once (by version number)

Follow `AGENTS.md` and the skills `start-next-version`, `work-on-issue`, `finish-version`, `release-version`, `deploy-version`, `plan-work`, `version-status`. "The next version" is what `composer milestone:next` prints. Ask the ship-gate question before any merge into `main`, tag, release or deploy.

## Never

- Force-push, `git reset --hard` or rebase a shared branch, or squash into `main`.
- Delete issues or milestones, rename milestones, or change labels other than `area:` labels.
- Print or commit tokens, `.env` contents, `APP_KEY` or credentials.
- Add paid or third-party security scanners; use only free GitHub features.
